he  tax Bush tax breaks for the wealthy and  in fact also even lowered the tax rates  on estate taxes for the top three tenths  of one percent and what I said if when  you had in December a Democratic  president a Democratic Senate and then a  democratic house if you couldn't win  under those political circumstances how  in God's name but we got to win when  right-wing Republicans were controlling  the house unfortunately that is exactly  what happened in the Democrats have been  caving in and caving in since I think  most people do understand that so where  we are right now I think with our mop  the mystical pessimistic I think the  American people have to stand up very  clearly all over this country and say no  no you're not going to cut Social  Security let's be clear you know this  so-called chained CPI which they're  talking about you go out and you tell  seen yesterday do it say oh by the way  there are folks in Washington who think  your Cola today which you have not  received the last two years despite the  fact that your prescription drug costs  than your health care costs of risen  they think that's too generous and what  they want to do is wait if you're 65 now  when you're 75 take back about five  hundred and sixty dollars that otherwise  would have gotten and when you're 85 a  thousand dollars see how seniors feel  about that so this division on fiscal  policy between Democrats and Republicans  so deeply entrenched can we expect this  to carry on right into  the election campaign can Americans  expect many more months of this sort of  confrontation because both parties seem  intent on hashing this out right into  the campaign make and making the  election almost a referendum on their  positions is that your expectation well  I well I I think the truth is you have  very very different philosophies and  while needless to say I strongly  strongly strongly disagree with the  Republican ideology which is designed in  my view to protect the wealthiest people 