ing that's coming down the pike  down the road trade legislation or  something that you're eyeing up that  you're saying I'm not going to stand for  it I'm going to go back to the floor and  I'm going to filibuster again well I  don't know that I'm gonna be  filibustering again but you are going to  hear my voice very loudly I think on  a couple of issues number one it's very  important that ordinary Americans stand  up right now in every one of our 50  states and say to the Congress say to  the supercommittee say to the president  that the negotiations that are taking  place right now with regard to deficit  reduction be fair that this committee  not come up with the proposal that  continues to go after some of the most  vulnerable people in this country that's  issue number one and the trade issue i  think is enormous it's not something  that is discussed very much in the  corporate media because there's a  general consensus that corporate media  likes unfettered free trade but i think  if you go to grassroots america and you  ask people whether nafta cafta permanent  normal trade relations with china has  worked for the middle class and working  class in this country they will tell you  no one hasn't so that's another issue  that i will be a pretty active on you  you said senator that you're not here to  beat up on president obama but you have  in the past talked about a primary  challenge to president obama and spoken  approvingly of one and i'm wondering if  you know who you have in mind for that  challenge and what you think that that  might accomplish if well what no i don't  have I don't know of anybody in mind but  I'm sure that there are serious and  smart people out there who can do it  here's the point if you're asking me do  I think at the end of the day that  Barack Obama is going to be the  Democratic candidate for president in  2012 I do but do I believe that it is a  good idea for our democracy and for the  Democratic body and I speak by the way  as